# TCP Analysis Notes — Project #3

## Lab 3-TCP Retrans.pcapng
- Opened in Wireshark on Kali
- Total Packets: 202
- File Size: 202 KB
- Observation: High-volume capture suitable for SOC-level analysis
- Protocols:
  - TCP: 202
  - UDP: 202
  - HTTP: 2
  - Media Type: 1
- Top Endpoints: A ↔ B (202 packets)
- Filters Applied:
  - `tcp.analysis.retransmission` → 3 retransmissions detected
  - `tcp.analysis.duplicate_ack` → duplicate ACKs observed
  - `tcp.analysis.zero_window` → zero window detected
  - `tcp.flags.reset == 1` → connection resets observed
- Notes: Minor retransmissions, flow control events, connection stability issues

## Lab 6-TCPResets.pcapng
- Filter Applied: `tcp.flags.reset == 1`
- Observation: Abrupt connection terminations observed; server/client reset behavior

## CLI Validation (Lab 3)
Command
"tshark -r Lab3-TCP\ Retrans.pcapng -q -z io,stat,1"
Observation: Traffic spikes per second identified; confirms retransmission bursts

## General Notes
- Analysis performed on local Kali VM
- All screenshots demonstrate SOC workflow:
  - Capture Properties
  - Protocol Hierarchy
